#~ msgid "**vCPU Placement**"
#~ msgstr "**vCPU Placement**"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "vCPU placement settings relate to vCPU"
#~ " placement within the physical topology "
#~ "of the CPU. Since a vCPU is "
#~ "just a schedulable thread the hypervisor"
#~ " maps onto physical cores, performance "
#~ "increases can be achieved through smart"
#~ " scheduling. A simplified CPU topology "
#~ "looks like this:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "vCPU placement configuraciones relate a "
#~ "vCPU placement dentro de el physical "
#~ "topology del CPU. Desde un vCPU es"
#~ " solo un schedulable thread el "
#~ "hypervisor mapea onto physical núcleos, "
#~ "rendimiento increases puede be achieved "
#~ "a través de smart scheduling. Un "
#~ "simplified CPU topology looks like este:"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Socket\n"
#~ " └── NUMA node\n"
#~ "     └── Core\n"
#~ "         └── Threads (SMT / Hyper-Threading)"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Socket\n"
#~ " └── NUMA nodo\n"
#~ "     └── Core\n"
#~ "         └── Threads (SMT / Hyper-Threading)"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Multiple physical cores can reside "
#~ "within the same NUMA node. Physical "
#~ "CPU cores within the same NUMA "
#~ "node share the same region of the"
#~ " L3 cache and local memory access."
#~ " By scheduling vCPUs making up a "
#~ "single VM to cores within the same"
#~ " NUMA node, you can avoid the "
#~ "performance penalties associated with crossing"
#~ " NUMA boundaries and accessing remote "
#~ "memory locations."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Múltiples physical núcleos puede reside "
#~ "dentro de el mismo NUMA nodo. "
#~ "Physical CPU núcleos dentro de el "
#~ "mismo NUMA nodo share el mismo "
#~ "región del L3 cache y local "
#~ "memoria acceso. Por scheduling vCPUs "
#~ "making up un single VM a núcleos"
#~ " dentro de el mismo NUMA nodo, "
#~ "you puede avoid el rendimiento penalties"
#~ " asociado con crossing NUMA boundaries "
#~ "y accessing remoto memoria locations."

#~ msgid "|clusters| offer three vCPU placement settings:"
#~ msgstr "|clusters| offer three vCPU placement configuraciones:"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Unmanaged** (default): The cluster makes "
#~ "no special effort to schedule vCPUs "
#~ "within the same NUMA region."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "**Unmanaged** (predeterminado): El cluster "
#~ "hace no special effort a schedule "
#~ "vCPUs dentro de el mismo NUMA "
#~ "región."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Region:** The cluster attempts to "
#~ "schedule vCPUs associated with the same"
#~ " VM within the same NUMA region. "
#~ "When flexibility is needed, vCPUs may"
#~ " hop to different physical cores but"
#~ " they will be kept within the "
#~ "same NUMA region."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "**Region:** El cluster attempts a "
#~ "schedule vCPUs asociado con el mismo "
#~ "VM dentro de el mismo NUMA región."
#~ " Cuando flexibility es necesario, vCPUs "
#~ "puede hop a diferente physical núcleos"
#~ " pero they será be kept dentro "
#~ "de el mismo NUMA región."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Pinned:** The cluster also attempts to"
#~ " schedule vCPUs associated with the "
#~ "same VM within the same NUMA "
#~ "region but the vCPUs will remain "
#~ "pinned to the same cores. In "
#~ "certain cases, pinning may improve "
#~ "performance and in other cases creating"
#~ " inflexibility may introduce inefficiency."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "**Pinned:** El cluster también attempts "
#~ "a schedule vCPUs asociado con el "
#~ "mismo VM dentro de el mismo NUMA"
#~ " región pero el vCPUs será remain "
#~ "pinned al mismo núcleos. En certain "
#~ "cases, pinning puede improve rendimiento "
#~ "y en otro cases creating inflexibility"
#~ " puede introduce inefficiency."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Setting **Region** placement is a "
#~ "sensible starting configuration if you "
#~ "don't have a specific reason to "
#~ "choose one of the other two. In"
#~ " internal testing, a 7-10% improvement "
#~ "in prime number generation time was "
#~ "observed with Region pinning versus "
#~ "Unmanaged pinning."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Setting **Region** placement es un "
#~ "sensible starting configuración si you "
#~ "don't tienen un específico reason a "
#~ "elegir one del otro two. En "
#~ "interno testing, un 7-10% improvement en"
#~ " prime número generation tiempo fue "
#~ "observed con Region pinning versus "
#~ "Unmanaged pinning."

